{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Who satisfies</b> — the meaning: for the healer is HaShem alone, and He is the one who satisfies him according to the knowledge of a physician, that he should eat thus and not eat thus." "The meaning of <b>who satisfies</b> — for the judgment of the sick person is to diminish his life's bread." "And the meaning of <b>your mouth</b> — your mouth, like עדיו (his ornaments), to restrain. And in my opinion: just as the soul is the glory of the body, so it is like an ornament. And so the meaning is: who satisfies with good your soul, corresponding to 'my soul shall be satisfied.'" "And the meaning of <b>renewed like the eagle, your youth</b> — Rabbi Moses said: for it is deficient yod, after the manner of ותעשי הרעות and ותוכל. And some say: for the eagle, the more it grows and advances in years, its bone grows stronger, and so it is: תתחדשי — your youth's bones are renewed like an eagle. And it is possible that the word נעוריכי is like נשים (feminine), and תתחדש comes accordingly, after the manner of 'בנות צעדה עלי שור.' And he mentioned youth in the construct state, like 'he will return to the days of his youth.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {3 "The word נעוריכי in Ibn Ezra's text apparently points to a defective spelling of נעוריך (your youth); the feminine parsing explanation is retained literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:01.582730640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}